notes:
Mapping decisions:
- language_switch per_question: questions are set in English and Hindi (except the English parts) (notice paras 13.8.1 and 13.9.7, PDF pp.25, 28).
- calculator left unset: the notice does not state it.
- numeric_input left unset: the paper has no numeric-entry questions, and the schema requires a value (schema change requested).
- qualifying left unset: the rule (minimum_percent_by_category) depends on category or on the Commission, which the schema cannot express (schema change requested).
- instructions: summary in our own words of the notice paragraphs cited in the source; Hindi translated.

Open questions:
- The notice is printed in English and Hindi (para 23(a), PDF p.48), but only the English notice was retrieved. Hindi titles here are translations (title_hi_source: translated); replace them with the official Hindi wording.
- Normalisation of multi-shift scores follows the SSC procedure published in the Notice dated 02-06-2025 (para 13.2, PDF p.24). That notice was not retrieved, so scoring.normalization only names it.
- The notice does not say whether a calculator (on-screen or physical) is allowed. calculator stays null.
- Shift timings are not stated in the notice; they appear on the Admission Certificate. shift_timings stays null.
- The number of options per question is not stated in the notice. options_per_question stays null.
- Tier-II dates: the notice only says 'December, 2026' (tentative).

